    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0077" n="17" xml:id="pg17"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Hale.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 127.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch of the 27th of August, No. 145, which is accompanied by the answer of
                    the Spanish government to the complaint which you submitted to it of ill
                    treatment to the officers and crew of the United States steamer Canandaigua, by
                    the sanitary authorities at Port Mahon.</p>
                <p>The explanations and assurances of the Spanish government are quite
                    satisfactory.</p>
                <p>You will please give a copy of this dispatch to the minister for foreign
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John P. Hale</hi> Esq.,<hi rendition="#italic">
                            &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d23-a1.xml" xpointer="d23-a1"/>
            </div>
